<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Saja_Records> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Saja Records** is a [LeFrak-Moelis Records](:LeFrak-Moelis_Records) subsidiary.It formerly holds the rights to [Jim Croce's](:Jim_Croce) [ABC-Dunhill](:ABC_Dunhill_Records) releases and currently the rights of [Stevie B](:Stevie_B)'s recordings before he signed with Empire Musicwerks. It is distributed by [Atlantic Records](:Atlantic_Records).In 2012, Saja relinquished the rights of Jim Croce's ABC-Dunhill discography to [Disney Music Group](:Disney_Music_Group) of [The Walt Disney Company](:The_Walt_Disney_Company); those albums will be re-issued by [Hollywood Records](:Hollywood_Records) except **\"[I Got a Name](:I_Got_a_Name)\"**, which will be re-released by [Walt Disney Records](:Walt_Disney_Records) because the [title song of the album](:I_Got_a_Name_%28song%29) was featured in the soundtrack of the 2006 film \"[Invincible](:Invincible_%282006_film%29)\". Disney Music Group is currently sister of the [American Broadcasting Company](:American_Broadcasting_Company), the former parent of ABC-Dunhill, and is distributed by the label's successor company [Universal Music Group](:Universal_Music_Group) (which owns Croce's [Capitol Records](:Capitol_Records) discography outright)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
