<http://dbpedia.org/resource/The_Hertz_Corporation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**The Hertz Corporation** is an American [car rental](:Car_rental) company based in [Estero, Florida](:Estero%2C_Florida). The company operates its namesake Hertz brand, along with the brands [Dollar Rent A Car](:Dollar_Rent_A_Car), [Firefly Car Rental](:Firefly_Car_Rental) and [Thrifty Car Rental](:Thrifty_Car_Rental).It is one of the three big rental car holding companies in the United States, holding a 36% market share, placing it ahead of both [Enterprise Holdings](:Enterprise_Holdings) and the [Avis Budget Group](:Avis_Budget_Group). As one of the largest worldwide vehicle rental companies by sales, locations, and fleet size, Hertz operates in 160 countries in North America, Europe, Latin America, Africa, Asia, Australia, the Caribbean, the Middle East and New Zealand.Hertz was ranked 326th in the 2020 [*Fortune* 500](:Fortune_500) list. The company filed for bankruptcy on May 22, 2020, citing a sharp decline in revenue and future bookings caused by the [COVID-19 pandemic](:COVID-19_pandemic). As of December 31, 2021, the company had revenues of $7.3 billion, assets of $19.7 billion, and 23,000 employees. As of July 1, 2021, the company is no longer in [Chapter 11 bankruptcy](:Chapter_11_Bankruptcy)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
