<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Společnost_s_ručením_omezeným> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Společnost s ručením omezeným (lit. ‘company with limited liability’) is the Czech and Slovak legal structure for a private limited company (as it is known in the UK) or a LLC (as it is known in the United States). The commercial name of a limited liability company must include the designation “společnost s ručením omezeným” (Czech) or “spoločnosť s ručením obmedzeným” (Slovak), (e.g. “limited liability company”), or in abbreviated forms, to wit: “spol. s r. o.” or “s. r. o.”.Foreign investors have no restrictions on setting up a limited liability company in the Czech Republic."@en .
