<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Wrocław> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Wrocław (Polish: [ˈvrɔt͡swaf]; German: Breslau, pronounced [ˈbʁɛslaʊ̯]; Silesian German: Brassel) is a city in southwestern Poland and the largest city in the historical region of Silesia. It lies on the banks of the River Oder in the Silesian Lowlands of Central Europe, roughly 350 kilometres (220 mi) from the Baltic Sea to the north and 40 kilometres (25 mi) from the Sudeten Mountains to the south. As of 2022, the official population of Wrocław is 672,929, with a total of 1.25 million residing in the metropolitan area, making it the third largest city in Poland."@en .
