<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Private_equity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Private equity (PE) typically refers to investment funds, generally organized as limited partnerships, that buy and restructure companies. More formally, private equity is a type of equity and one of the asset classes consisting of equity securities and debt in operating companies that are not publicly traded on a stock exchange. Private equity is also often grouped into a broader category called \"private capital\", generally used to describe capital supporting any long-term, illiquid investment strategy."@en .
