<http://dbpedia.org/resource/T-Bones_Records> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "T-Bones Records is a record label founded by producer (aka \"\"). The label was born in Hattiesburg, Mississippi when Ramenofsky was a member of the metal fusion band Loppybogymi. In 2000, Ramenofsky discovered rapper Afroman and produced the album, \"Because I Got High\". The record was originally released on T-Bones Records. The title track was soon posted on file-sharing service Napster and made it to The Howard Stern Show. This song was the theme song of the film Jay and Silent Bob Strike Back and was later featured in the films Disturbia and The Perfect Score. \"Because I Got High\" was nominated for the Grammy Award for Best Rap Solo Performance in 2002."@en .
