<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Golden,_Colorado> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Golden** is a [home rule city](:List_of_municipalities_in_Colorado%23Home_rule_municipality) that is the [county seat](:County_seat) of [Jefferson County](:Jefferson_County%2C_Colorado), [Colorado](:Colorado), United States. The city population was 20,399 at the [2020 United States Census](:2020_United_States_Census). Golden lies along [Clear Creek](:Clear_Creek_%28Colorado%29) at the base of the [Front Range](:Front_Range) of the [Rocky Mountains](:Rocky_Mountains). Founded during the [Pike's Peak Gold Rush](:Pike%27s_Peak_Gold_Rush) on June 16, 1859, the mining camp was originally named **Golden City** in honor of [Thomas L. Golden](:Thomas_L%2E_Golden). Golden City served as the capital of the provisional [Territory of Jefferson](:Territory_of_Jefferson) from 1860 to 1861, and capital of the official [Territory of Colorado](:Territory_of_Colorado) from 1862 to 1867. In 1867, the territorial capital was moved about 12 miles (19 km) east to [Denver City](:Denver%23History). Golden is now a part of the [Denver–Aurora–Lakewood, CO Metropolitan Statistical Area](:Denver%E2%80%93Aurora%E2%80%93Lakewood%2C_CO_Metropolitan_Statistical_Area) and the [Front Range Urban Corridor](:Front_Range_Urban_Corridor).The [Colorado School of Mines](:Colorado_School_of_Mines), offering programs in [engineering](:Engineering) and [science](:Science), is located in Golden. In addition, it is also home to the [National Renewable Energy Laboratory](:National_Renewable_Energy_Laboratory), [National Earthquake Information Center](:National_Earthquake_Information_Center), [Coors Brewing Company](:Coors_Brewing_Company), [CoorsTek](:CoorsTek), [Boston Market](:Boston_Market), [Spyderco](:Spyderco), [Software Bisque](:Software_Bisque), American Mountaineering Center, and [Colorado Railroad Museum](:Colorado_Railroad_Museum). It is the birthplace of the [Jolly Rancher](:Jolly_Rancher), a candy bought out by the [Hershey Foods Corporation](:Hershey_Foods_Corporation), and home to [Yeti Cycles](:Yeti_Cycles). Western showman [William F. \"Buffalo Bill\" Cody](:Buffalo_Bill) is buried nearby on [Lookout Mountain](:Lookout_Mountain_%28Colorado%29)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
