<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Mesa_Air_Group> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Mesa Air Group, Inc.** is a [Nevada Corporation](:Nevada_Corporation) commercial aviation [holding company](:Holding_company) with headquarters in Suite 700 at 410 North 44th Street in the [Camelback East](:Camelback_East) area of [Phoenix](:Phoenix%2C_Arizona), [Arizona](:Arizona), United States. The company operates one regional airline subsidiary: [Mesa Airlines](:Mesa_Airlines) which operates as American Eagle and United Express under contractual agreements with American Airlines and United Airlines respectively.Mesa was founded on a mesa in Farmington, New Mexico in 1982 by Larry and Janie Risley, a husband and wife team that mortgaged their home to finance their dream to own an airline. Mesa moved its headquarters to Phoenix, Arizona in 1998.As of June 2022, Mesa operated 167 aircraft, with more than 457 daily departures to 120 cities throughout the U.S., District of Columbia, Canada, Mexico, The Bahamas, and Cuba."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
