<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Wrought_Iron_Bridge_Company> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Wrought Iron Bridge Company was a bridge fabrication and construction company based in Canton, Ohio, United States. It specialized in the fabrication of iron truss bridges and was a prolific bridge builder in the late 19th century. It was one of the 28 firms consolidated by J. P. Morgan into the American Bridge Company in 1900. Many of its bridges have been listed on the National Register of Historic Places."@en .
