<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Tehran> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Tehran** (; Template:Lang-fa *Tehrân* Template:IPA-fa is the largest city in [Tehran Province](:Tehran_Province) and the [capital](:Capital_city) of [Iran](:Iran). With a population of around 9 million in the city and 15 million in the larger metropolitan area of [Greater Tehran](:Greater_Tehran), Tehran is the [most populous city](:List_of_largest_cities_of_Iran) in Iran and [Western Asia](:Western_Asia), and has the [second-largest metropolitan area](:Largest_metropolitan_areas_of_the_Middle_East) in the Middle East, after [Cairo](:Cairo). It is ranked 24th in the world by metropolitan area population.In the [Classical era](:Classical_antiquity), part of the territory of present-day Tehran was occupied by [Rhages](:Ray%2C_Iran), a prominent [Median](:Medes) city destroyed in the medieval [Arab](:Muslim_conquest_of_Persia), [Turkic](:Oghuz_Turks), and [Mongol](:Mongol_conquest_of_Khwarezmia) invasions. Modern Ray is an urban area absorbed into the metropolitan area of Greater Tehran.Tehran was first chosen as the capital of Iran by [Agha Mohammad Khan](:Agha_Mohammad_Khan_Qajar) of the [Qajar dynasty](:Qajar_dynasty) in 1786, because of its proximity to Iran's territories in the [Caucasus](:Caucasus), then separated from Iran in the [Russo-Iranian Wars](:Russo-Persian_Wars), to avoid the vying factions of the previously ruling Iranian dynasties. The capital has been moved several times throughout history, and Tehran is the [32nd national capital of Persia](:Capitals_of_Persia). Large-scale demolition and rebuilding began in the 1920s, and Tehran has been a destination for mass migrations from all over Iran since the 20th century.Tehran is home to many historical locations, including the royal complexes of [Golestan](:Golestan_Palace), [Sa'dabad](:Sa%27dabad_Complex), and [Niavaran](:Niavaran_Complex), where the two last dynasties of the former Imperial State of Iran were seated. Tehran's most famous landmarks include the [Azadi Tower](:Azadi_Tower), a memorial built under the reign of [Mohammad Reza Shah](:Mohammad_Reza_Pahlavi) of the [Pahlavi dynasty](:Pahlavi_dynasty) in 1971 to mark the [2,500th anniversary](:2%2C500-year_celebration_of_the_Persian_Empire) of the founding of the Imperial State of Iran, and the [Milad Tower](:Milad_Tower), the world's [sixth-tallest self-supporting tower](:List_of_tallest_towers), completed in 2007, and the Tabiat Bridge, completed in 2014.Most of the population are [Persian](:Persian_people), and roughly 99% of them understand and speak the [Persian language](:Persian_language), but large populations of [other ethnolinguistic groups](:Ethnicities_in_Iran) live in Tehran and speak Persian as a second language.Tehran has an international airport ([Imam Khomeini Airport](:Tehran_Imam_Khomeini_International_Airport%29), a domestic airport ([Mehrabad Airport](:Mehrabad_International_Airport%29), [a central railway station](:Tehran_railway_station), a [rapid transit](:Rapid_transit) system, [Tehran Metro](:Tehran_Metro), a [bus rapid transit](:Bus_rapid_transit) system, [trolleybuses](:Trolleybuses_in_Tehran), and [a large network of highways](:List_of_Expressways_in_Tehran).Plans to relocate Iran's capital from Tehran to another area, due to [air pollution](:Air_pollution) and earthquakes, have so far not yet received approval. A 2016 survey of 230 cities across the globe by consultant [Mercer](:Mercer_%28consulting_firm%29) ranked Tehran 203rd for [quality of life](:Quality_of_life). According to the [Global Destinations Cities Index](:Tourism%23MasterCard_Global_Destination_Cities_Index) in 2016, Tehran is among the top ten fastest [growing destinations](:Tourism_in_Iran).The City Council declared October 6 Tehran Day in 2016, celebrating the day in 1907 when the city officially became the capital of Iran."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
