<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Olde_Lockeford_Winery> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Olde Lockeford Winery is a winery and custom crush facility in Lockeford, California, United States. The winery was founded in 1946 as the Lockeford Cooperative Winery, but had closed more than a decade before being purchased by Don Litchfield in 1998. The winery complex was renamed , and reconfigured to house multiple \"micro-wineries\". Olde Lockeford Winery is one of several wineries in the complex. In addition to the wineries that lease space in the Vino Piazza, the facility also offers a custom crush facility that can be leased by winery operations in other parts of the state."@en .
