<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Wrought_Iron_Bridge_Company> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The **Wrought Iron Bridge Company** was a bridge fabrication and construction company based in [Canton](:Canton%2C_Ohio), [Ohio](:Ohio), [United States](:United_States). It specialized in the fabrication of iron [truss bridges](:Truss_bridge) and was a prolific bridge builder in the late 19th century. It was one of the 28 firms consolidated by [J. P. Morgan](:J%2E_P%2E_Morgan) into the [American Bridge Company](:American_Bridge_Company) in 1900. Many of its bridges have been listed on the [National Register of Historic Places](:National_Register_of_Historic_Places)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
