<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Saunderson_Tractor_and_Implement_Co.> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "H P Saunderson founded his Saunderson Tractor and Implement Company in Elstow, Bedford in 1890 after visiting Canada and seeing the Massey and Harris companies. In 1898 Saunderson demonstrated a \"Self Moving Vehicle\" at a trial organised at the Royal Show which it unfortunately failed to complete because of engine failure. It was priced at £250 but it is not known if any were sold. At this time it was the largest tractor company in the world, but went to be sold to a larger, vehicle manufacturing company."@en .
