<http://dbpedia.org/resource/My_Baggage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "My Baggage, formerly known as Uni Baggage, is a luggage delivery company which was established at the end of 2009 by Paul Stewart. The service is used mainly by students, expats, holidaymakers, travel nomads, sports teams, armed forces, and people moving abroad. It arranges the collection and delivery of its customers’ items through major couriers for a lower cost compared to customers booking transportation directly."@en .
<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Aylesbury> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Aylesbury (/ˈeɪlzbəri/ AYLZ-bər-ee) is the county town of Buckinghamshire, South East England. It is home to the Roald Dahl Children's Gallery and the Waterside Theatre. It is in central Buckinghamshire, midway between High Wycombe and Milton Keynes. Aylesbury was awarded Garden Town status in 2017. The housing target for the town is set to grow with 16,000 homes set to be built by 2033."@en .
