<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Richard_Metcalfe> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Richard Metcalfe** (born 21 November 1973 in [Leeds](:Leeds), [England](:England%29) is a former Scottish [rugby union](:Rugby_union) player. He was the world's tallest ever international rugby player. At 7 feet (213 cm), Metcalfe was about six inches taller than a typical second row forward, giving him considerable presence at the front of the [line-out](:Line-out_%28rugby_union%29).He won 13 Scotland caps between 2000 and 2001 and played for the [Newcastle Falcons](:Newcastle_Falcons) and [Northampton Saints](:Northampton_Saints). At [Newcastle Falcons](:Newcastle_Falcons) he made 6 appearances for the Falcons the season they won the [1997-98 Premiership](:1997%E2%80%9398_English_Premiership_%28rugby_union%29), and at Northampton he played in every game apart from the final for which he was a replacement (due to injury) in the victorious [2000 Heineken Cup Final](:2000_Heineken_Cup_Final) as they defeated [Munster](:Munster_Rugby). In 2003, however, his contract with the Borders/SRU was terminated and he retired after he suffered a long-term [knee](:Knee) injury."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
