<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Filmmaking> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Filmmaking (film production) is the process by which a motion picture is . Filmmaking involves a number of complex and discrete stages, starting with an initial story, idea, or commission. It then continues through screenwriting, casting, pre-production, shooting, sound recording, post-production, and screening the finished product before an audience that may result in a film release and an exhibition. Filmmaking occurs in a variety of economic, social, and political contexts around the world. It uses a variety of technologies and cinematic techniques."@en .
