<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Liquefied_petroleum_gas> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Liquefied petroleum gas (LPG or LP gas) is a fuel gas which contains a flammable mixture of hydrocarbon gases, specifically propane and butane. LPG is used as a fuel gas in heating appliances, cooking equipment, and vehicles. It is increasingly used as an aerosol propellant and a refrigerant, replacing chlorofluorocarbons in an effort to reduce damage to the ozone layer. When specifically used as a vehicle fuel, it is often referred to as autogas or even just as gas. A full LPG cylinder contains 86% liquid; the ullage volume will contain vapour at a pressure that varies with temperature."@en .
