<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Charlotte,_North_Carolina> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Charlotte** ( [*SHAR-lət*](:Help%3APronunciation_respelling_key%29) is the [most populous city](:List_of_municipalities_in_North_Carolina) in the [U.S. state](:U%2ES%2E_state) of [North Carolina](:North_Carolina). Located in the [Piedmont](:Piedmont_%28United_States%29) region, it is the [county seat](:County_seat) of [Mecklenburg County](:Mecklenburg_County%2C_North_Carolina). The population was 874,579 as of the [2020 census](:2020_United_States_census), making Charlotte the [16th-most populous city](:List_of_United_States_cities_by_population) in the U.S., the seventh most populous city in [the South](:Southern_United_States), and the second most populous city in the [Southeast](:Southeastern_United_States) behind [Jacksonville, Florida](:Jacksonville%2C_Florida). The city is the cultural, economic, and transportation center of the [Charlotte metropolitan area](:Charlotte_metropolitan_area), whose 2020 population of 2,660,329 ranked [22nd in the U.S](:List_of_metropolitan_statistical_areas).  [Metrolina](:Charlotte_metropolitan_area) is part of a sixteen-county market region or [combined statistical area](:Combined_statistical_area) with a 2020 census-estimated population of 2,846,550.Between 2004 and 2014, Charlotte was ranked as the country's fastest-growing metro area, with 888,000 new residents. Based on U.S. Census data from 2005 to 2015, Charlotte tops the U.S. in millennial population growth. It is the third-fastest-growing major city in the United States. Residents are referred to as \"[Charlotteans](:List_of_people_from_Charlotte%2C_North_Carolina)\".Charlotte is home to the corporate headquarters of [Bank of America](:Bank_of_America), [Truist Financial](:Truist_Financial), and the [east coast](:East_Coast_of_the_United_States) headquarters of [Wells Fargo](:Wells_Fargo), which along with other financial institutions has made it the second-largest banking center in the United States. As of 2020, Charlotte was considered as a [Gamma + level](:Globalization_and_World_Cities_Research_Network) [global city](:Global_city) by the [GaWC](:Globalization_and_World_Cities_Research_Network).Among Charlotte's notable attractions, some of the most popular include the [Carolina Panthers](:Carolina_Panthers) (NFL), the [Charlotte Hornets](:Charlotte_Hornets) (NBA), [Charlotte FC](:Charlotte_FC) (MLS), the [NASCAR Hall of Fame](:NASCAR_Hall_of_Fame), the [Charlotte Ballet](:Charlotte_Ballet), Children's Theatre of Charlotte, [Mint Museum](:Mint_Museum), [Harvey B. Gantt Center](:Harvey_B%2E_Gantt_Center), [Bechtler Museum of Modern Art](:Bechtler_Museum_of_Modern_Art), the [Billy Graham Library](:Billy_Graham_Library), [Levine Museum of the New South](:Levine_Museum_of_the_New_South), [Charlotte Museum of History](:Charlotte_Museum_of_History), [Carowinds](:Carowinds) amusement park, and the [U.S. National Whitewater Center](:U%2ES%2E_National_Whitewater_Center).Charlotte has a [humid subtropical climate](:Humid_subtropical_climate). It is located several miles east of the [Catawba River](:Catawba_River) and southeast of [Lake Norman](:Lake_Norman), the largest man-made lake in North Carolina. [Lake Wylie](:Lake_Wylie) and [Mountain Island Lake](:Mountain_Island_Lake) are two smaller man-made lakes located near the city."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
