<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Andheri> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Andheri ([ən̪d̪ʱeɾiː]) is a locality in the western part of the city of Mumbai in India. Udayanagari, the name of a hill near the Mahakali caves, inspired the name Andheri. On the former islet of Versova, also known as Vasave, there was another cluster of native East Indians. Andheri east and west are key areas in Mumbai, with several film studios and TV news channels. high-profile police cases. Andheri west is covered by a fire complaint filed at the Oshiwara police station. MIDC, Andheri has a jewelry production unit (east)."@en .
