<http://dbpedia.org/resource/Xi'an> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "**Xi'an** ( [*shee-AN*](:Help%3APronunciation_respelling_key),  [*shee-AHN*](:Help%3APronunciation_respelling_key); [Chinese](:Chinese_language): 西安; [pinyin](:Pinyin): *Xī'ān*; Chinese:  ), frequently spelled as **Xian** and also known by [other names](:Xi%27an%23Name), is the [capital](:List_of_capitals_in_China) of [Shaanxi Province](:Shaanxi). A [sub-provincial city](:Sub-provincial_division%23Sub-provincial_municipalities) on the [Guanzhong Plain](:Guanzhong), the city is the third most populous city in [Western China](:Western_China), after [Chongqing](:Chongqing) and [Chengdu](:Chengdu), as well as the most populous city in [Northwest China](:Northwest_China). Its total population was 12,952,907 as of the 2020 census. The total urban population was 9.28 million.Since the 1980s, as part of the [economic growth of inland China](:China_Western_Development) especially for the central and northwest regions, Xi'an has re-emerged as a cultural, industrial, political and educational centre of the entire central-northwest region, with many facilities for [research and development](:Research_and_development). Xi'an currently holds [sub-provincial](:Sub-provincial_city_in_the_People%27s_Republic_of_China) status, administering 11 districts and 2 counties. In 2020, Xi'an was ranked as a Beta- (global second tier) city by the [Globalization and World Cities Research Network](:Globalization_and_World_Cities_Research_Network), and, according to the country's own ranking, ranked 17th. Xi'an is also one of the world's top 100 financial centers, according to the [Global Financial Centres Index](:Global_Financial_Centres_Index). Xi'an is ranked in the top [30](:List_of_cities_by_scientific_output) cities in the world by scientific research output as tracked by the [Nature Index](:Nature_Index), and home to multiple [China's prestige universities](:List_of_universities_and_colleges_in_Shaanxi) in [Northwest China](:Northwest_China), including [Xi'an Jiaotong University](:Xi%27an_Jiaotong_University), [Northwestern Polytechnical University](:Northwestern_Polytechnical_University), [Xidian University](:Xidian_University) and [Northwest University](:Northwest_University_%28China%29).Known as [Chang'an](:Chang%27an) in much of its history, Xi'an is one of the Chinese [Four Great Ancient Capitals](:Historical_capitals_of_China), having held the position under several of the most important [dynasties in Chinese history](:Dynasties_in_Chinese_history), including [Western Zhou](:Western_Zhou), [Western Han](:Western_Han), [Sui](:Sui_dynasty), [Northern Zhou](:Northern_Zhou) and [Tang](:Tang_dynasty). Xi'an is now the second most popular tourist destination in China. The city is the starting point of the [Silk Road](:Silk_Road) and home to the [Terracotta Army](:Terracotta_Army) of [Emperor Qin Shi Huang](:Emperor_Qin_Shi_Huang), both of which are listed as [UNESCO World Heritage sites](:UNESCO_World_Heritage_site)."^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
